{"uncertainty": 0.25, "outcome": "Delivered apb_gpio.v (rtl_source, top apb_gpio) and apb_gpio_tb.v (testbench, top apb_gpio_tb). Both are written to the approved interface and microarchitecture specs. No formal_spec is included, so the formal evidence requirements do not apply to this submission. Lint, simulation and synthesis are still to be run by the platform.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "APB4 GPIO completer with zero wait states, written to [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.microarchitecture.a1] against [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.interface-spec.a1], serving [requirement:req-837b82982d]. pready is tied high and access = psel && penable. A mapped address must be aligned, have no bits set above bit 5, and use index 0 to 8. pslverr is driven on unmapped accesses and on writes to DATA_IN. prdata is zero unless the cycle is a mapped read access. All registers are 32 bits, masked by a constant pin mask from a generate block. Writes merge with byte strobes. Detection uses two sample registers. Status is (status & ~clear) | detected, so a detection beats a clear. irq = |(status & INTR_ENABLE). Reset is synchronous and active low on every flop."}, {"kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed, self-checking testbench. It runs two instances at once, N=8 and N=32, as the verification plan in [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.microarchitecture.a1] asks, covering the list in section 8 of [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.interface-spec.a1]. Every failed check is reported with $error and passing checks are counted. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once before $finish, using the nirmaan_nonce plusarg."}], "files": [{"path": "apb_gpio.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "apb_gpio RTL", "summary": "Single-clock Verilog-2001 implementation of [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.microarchitecture.a1], meeting the ports, register map, detection, response and reset rules of [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.interface-spec.a1] for [requirement:req-837b82982d]. Combinational blocks give every output a default, and every case has a default. Sequential blocks use only nonblocking assignments. There are no zero-width replications at N=32. Design-intent assertions sit inside an ifdef FORMAL block.", "entry": "apb_gpio"}, {"path": "apb_gpio_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "apb_gpio testbench (N=8 and N=32)", "summary": "Testbench for [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.interface-spec.a1] section 8. It covers:\n- reset values, before and after a second reset;\n- every read/write register with partial strobes, no strobes, and bits above N;\n- gpio_out and gpio_oe;\n- DATA_IN as read-only with PSLVERR;\n- unmapped, unaligned and aliasing addresses, which must return zero, raise PSLVERR and change nothing;\n- back-to-back write then read;\n- rising-edge detection timing at edge E+1 (checked on irq), and an edge that fires only once;\n- falling edges and a one-cycle pulse;\n- a high level and a low level that set the status again after a clear;\n- write-1-to-clear of some bits only and of strobed bytes only;\n- a detection on the same edge as a clear, where the detection wins;\n- the interrupt mask, including the top pin.\nStimulus is driven at negedge, and expected values are computed in the testbench, as [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.microarchitecture.a1] describes.", "entry": "apb_gpio_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["The RTL and testbench have not been linted, simulated or synthesized by this seat; whether they are lint-clean, pass simulation and synthesize without latches is unknown until the platform runs lint.run, simulator.run and synth.run.", "Width-clean Verilator compilation of the testbench (default warnings fatal) is intended but not confirmed.", "The ifdef FORMAL assertions in apb_gpio.v are design intent only; no formal_spec was submitted, so they are not exercised."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Deviation from the plan in [artifact:prj-b3c686270a.microarchitecture.a1]: the verification plan lists apb_gpio.sby and apb_gpio_n32.sby, but this task's expected outputs are rtl_source and testbench only. No formal_spec was produced, and the formal proof should be tracked as follow-up work, for the tech lead to schedule.\n\nThe testbench expects gpio_in held stable through reset, with pins at 0.\n\nThe RTL supports ADDR_WIDTH=8 only, as the interface spec requires. The decode uses paddr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:6], which needs ADDR_WIDTH of 7 or more.\n\nThe timeout watchdog in the testbench is 2 ms of simulated time."}
=== FILE: apb_gpio.v ===
// apb_gpio.v -- APB4 GPIO peripheral with interrupts.
// Implements interface_spec.md through microarchitecture.md (task prj-b3c686270a:rtl-implementation).
// Zero wait states: pready is tied high, a transfer completes when psel && penable.
`timescale 1ns/1ps

module apb_gpio #(
    parameter integer ADDR_WIDTH = 8,
    parameter integer N          = 8
) (
    input  wire                  pclk,
    input  wire                  presetn,
    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] paddr,
    input  wire                  psel,
    input  wire                  penable,
    input  wire                  pwrite,
    input  wire [31:0]           pwdata,
    input  wire [3:0]            pstrb,
    output reg  [31:0]           prdata,
    output wire                  pready,
    output wire                  pslverr,
    input  wire [N-1:0]          gpio_in,
    output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_out,
    output wire [N-1:0]          gpio_oe,
    output wire                  irq
);

    // Register indices (paddr[5:2]).
    localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_OUT    = 4'd0;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_DIR         = 4'd1;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_DATA_IN     = 4'd2;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_RISE   = 4'd3;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_FALL   = 4'd4;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_HIGH   = 4'd5;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_LOW    = 4'd6;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_ENABLE = 4'd7;
    localparam [3:0] IDX_INTR_STATUS = 4'd8;

    // State.
    reg [31:0] data_out_q;
    reg [31:0] dir_q;
    reg [31:0] in_q;
    reg [31:0] in_prev_q;
    reg [31:0] rise_en_q;
    reg [31:0] fall_en_q;
    reg [31:0] high_en_q;
    reg [31:0] low_en_q;
    reg [31:0] ien_q;
    reg [31:0] status_q;

    // Constant pin mask (bits 0..N-1) and the input widened to 32 bits.
    wire [31:0] pin_mask;
    wire [31:0] in_ext;

    genvar g;
    generate
        for (g = 0; g < 32; g = g + 1) begin : g_bit
            if (g < N) begin : g_pin
                assign pin_mask[g] = 1'b1;
                assign in_ext[g]   = gpio_in[g];
            end else begin : g_nopin
                assign pin_mask[g] = 1'b0;
                assign in_ext[g]   = 1'b0;
            end
        end
    endgenerate

    // APB decode.
    wire       access     = psel & penable;
    wire [3:0] reg_idx    = paddr[5:2];
    wire       addr_align = (paddr[1:0] == 2'b00);
    wire       addr_high0 = (paddr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:6] == {(ADDR_WIDTH-6){1'b0}});
    wire       mapped     = addr_align & addr_high0 & (reg_idx <= IDX_INTR_STATUS);
    wire       wr_en      = access & pwrite & mapped;
    wire       rd_en      = access & ~pwrite & mapped;

    wire [31:0] wmask = {{8{pstrb[3]}}, {8{pstrb[2]}}, {8{pstrb[1]}}, {8{pstrb[0]}}} & pin_mask;

    wire we_data_out = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_DATA_OUT);
    wire we_dir      = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_DIR);
    wire we_rise     = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_RISE);
    wire we_fall     = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_FALL);
    wire we_high     = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_HIGH);
    wire we_low      = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_LOW);
    wire we_ien      = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_ENABLE);
    wire we_status   = wr_en & (reg_idx == IDX_INTR_STATUS);

    // Next state of the read/write registers: byte-strobe merge.
    wire [31:0] data_out_d = we_data_out ? ((data_out_q & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : data_out_q;
    wire [31:0] dir_d      = we_dir      ? ((dir_q      & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : dir_q;
    wire [31:0] rise_en_d  = we_rise     ? ((rise_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : rise_en_q;
    wire [31:0] fall_en_d  = we_fall     ? ((fall_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : fall_en_q;
    wire [31:0] high_en_d  = we_high     ? ((high_en_q  & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : high_en_q;
    wire [31:0] low_en_d   = we_low      ? ((low_en_q   & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : low_en_q;
    wire [31:0] ien_d      = we_ien      ? ((ien_q      & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask)) : ien_q;

    // Detection and write-1-to-clear status; detection wins over a clear.
    wire [31:0] rise_ev  = in_q & ~in_prev_q;
    wire [31:0] fall_ev  = ~in_q & in_prev_q;
    wire [31:0] detected = ((rise_ev & rise_en_q) | (fall_ev & fall_en_q)
                           | (in_q & high_en_q) | (~in_q & low_en_q)) & pin_mask;
    wire [31:0] clr      = we_status ? (pwdata & wmask) : 32'h0000_0000;
    wire [31:0] status_d = (status_q & ~clr) | detected;

    // Register block: synchronous active-low reset.
    always @(posedge pclk) begin
        if (!presetn) begin
            data_out_q <= 32'h0000_0000;
            dir_q      <= 32'h0000_0000;
            in_q       <= 32'h0000_0000;
            in_prev_q  <= 32'h0000_0000;
            rise_en_q  <= 32'h0000_0000;
            fall_en_q  <= 32'h0000_0000;
            high_en_q  <= 32'h0000_0000;
            low_en_q   <= 32'h0000_0000;
            ien_q      <= 32'h0000_0000;
            status_q   <= 32'h0000_0000;
        end else begin
            data_out_q <= data_out_d;
            dir_q      <= dir_d;
            in_q       <= in_ext;
            in_prev_q  <= in_q;
            rise_en_q  <= rise_en_d;
            fall_en_q  <= fall_en_d;
            high_en_q  <= high_en_d;
            low_en_q   <= low_en_d;
            ien_q      <= ien_d;
            status_q   <= status_d;
        end
    end

    // Read data: zero unless this is a mapped read access.
    always @(*) begin
        prdata = 32'h0000_0000;
        if (rd_en) begin
            case (reg_idx)
                IDX_DATA_OUT:    prdata = data_out_q;
                IDX_DIR:         prdata = dir_q;
                IDX_DATA_IN:     prdata = in_q;
                IDX_INTR_RISE:   prdata = rise_en_q;
                IDX_INTR_FALL:   prdata = fall_en_q;
                IDX_INTR_HIGH:   prdata = high_en_q;
                IDX_INTR_LOW:    prdata = low_en_q;
                IDX_INTR_ENABLE: prdata = ien_q;
                IDX_INTR_STATUS: prdata = status_q;
                default:         prdata = 32'h0000_0000;
            endcase
        end
    end

    assign pready   = 1'b1;
    assign pslverr  = access & (~mapped | (pwrite & (reg_idx == IDX_DATA_IN)));
    assign gpio_out = data_out_q[N-1:0];
    assign gpio_oe  = dir_q[N-1:0];
    assign irq      = |(status_q & ien_q);

`ifdef FORMAL
    // Design intent (not exercised by this submission).
    always @(*) begin
        assert (pready == 1'b1);
        if (!access) begin
            assert (prdata == 32'h0000_0000);
            assert (pslverr == 1'b0);
        end
    end
`endif

endmodule
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: apb_gpio_tb.v ===
// apb_gpio_tb.v -- self-checking testbench for apb_gpio, at N = 8 and N = 32.
// Stimulus is driven after the falling edge; combinational outputs are checked
// 1 ns later, before the next rising edge.
`timescale 1ns/1ps

module apb_gpio_tb_core #(
    parameter integer N = 8
) (
    output reg        done,
    output reg [31:0] n_pass,
    output reg [31:0] n_fail
);
    localparam [7:0] A_DATA_OUT = 8'h00;
    localparam [7:0] A_DIR      = 8'h04;
    localparam [7:0] A_DATA_IN  = 8'h08;
    localparam [7:0] A_RISE     = 8'h0C;
    localparam [7:0] A_FALL     = 8'h10;
    localparam [7:0] A_HIGH     = 8'h14;
    localparam [7:0] A_LOW      = 8'h18;
    localparam [7:0] A_IEN      = 8'h1C;
    localparam [7:0] A_STAT     = 8'h20;
    localparam       OK         = 1'b0;
    localparam       ERR        = 1'b1;
    localparam [31:0] PINS = (N >= 32) ? 32'hFFFF_FFFF : ((32'h0000_0001 << N) - 32'h0000_0001);

    reg          pclk;
    reg          presetn;
    reg          psel;
    reg          penable;
    reg          pwrite;
    reg  [7:0]   paddr;
    reg  [31:0]  pwdata;
    reg  [3:0]   pstrb;
    reg  [N-1:0] gpio_in;
    wire [31:0]  prdata;
    wire         pready;
    wire         pslverr;
    wire [N-1:0] gpio_out;
    wire [N-1:0] gpio_oe;
    wire         irq;

    apb_gpio #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8), .N(N)) dut (
        .pclk(pclk), .presetn(presetn), .paddr(paddr), .psel(psel),
        .penable(penable), .pwrite(pwrite), .pwdata(pwdata), .pstrb(pstrb),
        .prdata(prdata), .pready(pready), .pslverr(pslverr),
        .gpio_in(gpio_in), .gpio_out(gpio_out), .gpio_oe(gpio_oe), .irq(irq)
    );

    initial pclk = 1'b0;
    always #5 pclk = ~pclk;

    // Shadow model of the read/write registers.
    reg [31:0] m_dout;
    reg [31:0] m_dir;
    reg [31:0] m_rise;
    reg [31:0] m_fall;
    reg [31:0] m_high;
    reg [31:0] m_low;
    reg [31:0] m_ien;

    reg [31:0] pat;
    reg [31:0] e;
    reg [31:0] hb;

    function [31:0] lanes;
        input [3:0] s;
        begin
            lanes = {{8{s[3]}}, {8{s[2]}}, {8{s[1]}}, {8{s[0]}}};
        end
    endfunction

    function is_rw;
        input [7:0] a;
        begin
            is_rw = (a == A_DATA_OUT) || (a == A_DIR) || (a == A_RISE) || (a == A_FALL)
                 || (a == A_HIGH) || (a == A_LOW) || (a == A_IEN);
        end
    endfunction

    function [31:0] model_value;
        input [7:0] a;
        begin
            case (a)
                A_DATA_OUT: model_value = m_dout;
                A_DIR:      model_value = m_dir;
                A_RISE:     model_value = m_rise;
                A_FALL:     model_value = m_fall;
                A_HIGH:     model_value = m_high;
                A_LOW:      model_value = m_low;
                A_IEN:      model_value = m_ien;
                default:    model_value = 32'h0000_0000;
            endcase
        end
    endfunction

    task model_write;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] d;
        input [3:0]  s;
        reg   [31:0] m;
        begin
            m = lanes(s) & PINS;
            case (a)
                A_DATA_OUT: m_dout = (m_dout & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_DIR:      m_dir  = (m_dir  & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_RISE:     m_rise = (m_rise & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_FALL:     m_fall = (m_fall & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_HIGH:     m_high = (m_high & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_LOW:      m_low  = (m_low  & ~m) | (d & m);
                A_IEN:      m_ien  = (m_ien  & ~m) | (d & m);
                default:    m_dout = m_dout;
            endcase
        end
    endtask

    task chk;
        input [31:0] got;
        input [31:0] exp;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            if (got === exp) begin
                n_pass = n_pass + 32'd1;
            end else begin
                n_fail = n_fail + 32'd1;
                $error("apb_gpio N=%0d check %0d failed at %0t: got 0x%h, expected 0x%h",
                       N, id, $time, got, exp);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task chk_pins;
        input [N-1:0] got;
        input [N-1:0] exp;
        input [31:0]  id;
        begin
            if (got === exp) begin
                n_pass = n_pass + 32'd1;
            end else begin
                n_fail = n_fail + 32'd1;
                $error("apb_gpio N=%0d pin check %0d failed at %0t: got 0x%h, expected 0x%h",
                       N, id, $time, got, exp);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task chk_irq;
        input        exp;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            chk({31'd0, irq}, {31'd0, exp}, id);
        end
    endtask

    task check_outs;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            chk_pins(gpio_out, m_dout[N-1:0], id);
            chk_pins(gpio_oe,  m_dir[N-1:0],  id + 32'd1);
        end
    endtask

    task idle_cycle;
        begin
            @(negedge pclk);
            psel    = 1'b0;
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b0;
            paddr   = 8'h00;
            pwdata  = 32'h0000_0000;
            pstrb   = 4'h0;
        end
    endtask

    task tick;
        input [31:0] n;
        reg   [31:0] k;
        begin
            for (k = 32'd0; k < n; k = k + 32'd1) idle_cycle;
        end
    endtask

    task set_pins;
        input [31:0] v;
        begin
            idle_cycle;
            gpio_in = v[N-1:0];
        end
    endtask

    task apb_wr;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] d;
        input [3:0]  s;
        input        exp_err;
        input        drive_pins;
        input [31:0] pv;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            @(negedge pclk);
            psel    = 1'b1;
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b1;
            paddr   = a;
            pwdata  = d;
            pstrb   = s;
            if (drive_pins) gpio_in = pv[N-1:0];
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, 32'd0, id);
            chk(prdata, 32'h0000_0000, id);
            @(negedge pclk);
            penable = 1'b1;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pready}, 32'd1, id);
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, {31'd0, exp_err}, id);
            chk(prdata, 32'h0000_0000, id);
            if (is_rw(a)) model_write(a, d, s);
            idle_cycle;
        end
    endtask

    task apb_write;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] d;
        input [3:0]  s;
        input        exp_err;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            apb_wr(a, d, s, exp_err, 1'b0, 32'h0000_0000, id);
        end
    endtask

    task apb_write_pins;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] d;
        input [3:0]  s;
        input        exp_err;
        input [31:0] pv;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            apb_wr(a, d, s, exp_err, 1'b1, pv, id);
        end
    endtask

    task apb_read;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] exp_data;
        input        exp_err;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            @(negedge pclk);
            psel    = 1'b1;
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b0;
            paddr   = a;
            pwdata  = 32'h0000_0000;
            pstrb   = 4'h0;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, 32'd0, id);
            chk(prdata, 32'h0000_0000, id);
            @(negedge pclk);
            penable = 1'b1;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pready}, 32'd1, id);
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, {31'd0, exp_err}, id);
            chk(prdata, exp_data, id);
            idle_cycle;
        end
    endtask

    // Write, then a read of the same address in the very next setup phase.
    task apb_b2b;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] d;
        input [3:0]  s;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            @(negedge pclk);
            psel    = 1'b1;
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b1;
            paddr   = a;
            pwdata  = d;
            pstrb   = s;
            @(negedge pclk);
            penable = 1'b1;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pready}, 32'd1, id);
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, 32'd0, id);
            if (is_rw(a)) model_write(a, d, s);
            @(negedge pclk);
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b0;
            pwdata  = 32'h0000_0000;
            pstrb   = 4'h0;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, 32'd0, id + 32'd1);
            chk(prdata, 32'h0000_0000, id + 32'd1);
            @(negedge pclk);
            penable = 1'b1;
            #1;
            chk({31'd0, pslverr}, 32'd0, id + 32'd2);
            chk(prdata, model_value(a), id + 32'd2);
            idle_cycle;
        end
    endtask

    task unmapped;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            apb_write(a, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, ERR, id);
            apb_read(a, 32'h0000_0000, ERR, id + 32'd1);
        end
    endtask

    task read_all_rw;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            apb_read(A_DATA_OUT, model_value(A_DATA_OUT), OK, id);
            apb_read(A_DIR,      model_value(A_DIR),      OK, id + 32'd1);
            apb_read(A_RISE,     model_value(A_RISE),     OK, id + 32'd2);
            apb_read(A_FALL,     model_value(A_FALL),     OK, id + 32'd3);
            apb_read(A_HIGH,     model_value(A_HIGH),     OK, id + 32'd4);
            apb_read(A_LOW,      model_value(A_LOW),      OK, id + 32'd5);
            apb_read(A_IEN,      model_value(A_IEN),      OK, id + 32'd6);
            check_outs(id + 32'd7);
        end
    endtask

    task read_all_zero;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            apb_read(A_DATA_OUT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, id);
            apb_read(A_DIR,      32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd1);
            apb_read(A_DATA_IN,  32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd2);
            apb_read(A_RISE,     32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd3);
            apb_read(A_FALL,     32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd4);
            apb_read(A_HIGH,     32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd5);
            apb_read(A_LOW,      32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd6);
            apb_read(A_IEN,      32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd7);
            apb_read(A_STAT,     32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd8);
            chk_pins(gpio_out, {N{1'b0}}, id + 32'd9);
            chk_pins(gpio_oe,  {N{1'b0}}, id + 32'd10);
            chk_irq(1'b0, id + 32'd11);
        end
    endtask

    task do_reset;
        input [31:0] id;
        begin
            @(negedge pclk);
            presetn = 1'b0;
            psel    = 1'b0;
            penable = 1'b0;
            pwrite  = 1'b0;
            paddr   = 8'h00;
            pwdata  = 32'h0000_0000;
            pstrb   = 4'h0;
            @(negedge pclk);
            @(negedge pclk);
            #1;
            chk_pins(gpio_out, {N{1'b0}}, id);
            chk_pins(gpio_oe,  {N{1'b0}}, id + 32'd1);
            chk_irq(1'b0, id + 32'd2);
            @(negedge pclk);
            presetn = 1'b1;
            m_dout  = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_dir   = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_rise  = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_fall  = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_high  = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_low   = 32'h0000_0000;
            m_ien   = 32'h0000_0000;
        end
    endtask

    // Strobe and upper-bit test of one read/write register.
    task rw_test;
        input [7:0]  a;
        input [31:0] id;
        reg   [31:0] x;
        begin
            apb_write(a, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, id);
            x = PINS;
            apb_read(a, x, OK, id + 32'd1);
            check_outs(id + 32'd2);

            apb_write(a, 32'h0000_0000, 4'b0101, OK, id + 32'd10);
            x = PINS & 32'hFF00_FF00;
            apb_read(a, x, OK, id + 32'd11);
            check_outs(id + 32'd12);

            apb_write(a, 32'h1234_5678, 4'b1010, OK, id + 32'd20);
            x = 32'h1200_5600 & PINS;
            apb_read(a, x, OK, id + 32'd21);
            check_outs(id + 32'd22);

            apb_write(a, 32'hA5A5_A5A5, 4'b0001, OK, id + 32'd30);
            x = 32'h1200_56A5 & PINS;
            apb_read(a, x, OK, id + 32'd31);
            check_outs(id + 32'd32);

            apb_write(a, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'b0000, OK, id + 32'd40);
            apb_read(a, x, OK, id + 32'd41);
            check_outs(id + 32'd42);

            apb_write(a, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, id + 32'd50);
            apb_read(a, 32'h0000_0000, OK, id + 32'd51);
            check_outs(id + 32'd52);
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        done    = 1'b0;
        n_pass  = 32'd0;
        n_fail  = 32'd0;
        presetn = 1'b0;
        psel    = 1'b0;
        penable = 1'b0;
        pwrite  = 1'b0;
        paddr   = 8'h00;
        pwdata  = 32'h0000_0000;
        pstrb   = 4'h0;
        gpio_in = {N{1'b0}};
        m_dout  = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_dir   = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_rise  = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_fall  = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_high  = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_low   = 32'h0000_0000;
        m_ien   = 32'h0000_0000;
        pat     = 32'h0000_0000;
        e       = 32'h0000_0000;
        hb      = 32'h0000_0001 << (N - 1);

        // T1: reset values.
        do_reset(32'd100);
        read_all_zero(32'd110);

        // T2: every read/write register, partial strobes, bits above N.
        rw_test(A_DATA_OUT, 32'd200);
        rw_test(A_DIR,      32'd300);
        rw_test(A_RISE,     32'd400);
        rw_test(A_FALL,     32'd500);
        rw_test(A_HIGH,     32'd600);
        rw_test(A_LOW,      32'd700);
        rw_test(A_IEN,      32'd800);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd900);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd901);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd902);

        // T3: DATA_IN sampling, read only.
        set_pins(32'h5A3C_96E1);
        apb_read(A_DATA_IN, 32'h5A3C_96E1 & PINS, OK, 32'd1000);
        apb_write(A_DATA_IN, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, ERR, 32'd1001);
        apb_write(A_DATA_IN, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, ERR, 32'd1002);
        apb_read(A_DATA_IN, 32'h5A3C_96E1 & PINS, OK, 32'd1003);
        read_all_rw(32'd1010);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1020);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        apb_read(A_DATA_IN, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1021);

        // T4: PSLVERR policy, unmapped and unaligned addresses, no aliasing.
        apb_write(A_DATA_OUT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1100);
        apb_write(A_DIR,      32'h0F0F_0F0F, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1101);
        apb_write(A_IEN,      32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1102);
        unmapped(8'h24, 32'd1110);
        unmapped(8'h28, 32'd1120);
        unmapped(8'h3C, 32'd1130);
        unmapped(8'h40, 32'd1140);
        unmapped(8'h44, 32'd1150);
        unmapped(8'h5C, 32'd1160);
        unmapped(8'h60, 32'd1170);
        unmapped(8'h80, 32'd1180);
        unmapped(8'hA0, 32'd1190);
        unmapped(8'hC4, 32'd1200);
        unmapped(8'hFC, 32'd1210);
        unmapped(8'h01, 32'd1220);
        unmapped(8'h02, 32'd1230);
        unmapped(8'h03, 32'd1240);
        unmapped(8'h05, 32'd1250);
        unmapped(8'h1E, 32'd1260);
        unmapped(8'h21, 32'd1270);
        unmapped(8'h23, 32'd1280);
        read_all_rw(32'd1300);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1310);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1311);
        apb_write(A_DATA_OUT, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1320);
        apb_write(A_DIR,      32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1321);
        apb_write(A_IEN,      32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1322);

        // Back-to-back transfers: setup straight after a completion.
        apb_b2b(A_DATA_OUT, 32'h3C3C_3C3C, 4'hF,    32'd1400);
        check_outs(32'd1405);
        apb_b2b(A_DIR,      32'hC3C3_C3C3, 4'b0011, 32'd1410);
        check_outs(32'd1415);
        apb_b2b(A_DATA_OUT, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF,    32'd1420);
        apb_b2b(A_DIR,      32'h0000_0000, 4'hF,    32'd1430);
        check_outs(32'd1440);

        // T5: rising edge, timing (sample on E, status on E+1), fires once.
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0003, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1500);
        apb_write(A_IEN,  32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1501);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1502);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0001);
        idle_cycle;
        #1;
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1503);
        idle_cycle;
        #1;
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd1504);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, OK, 32'd1505);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1506);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1507);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1508);
        tick(32'd3);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1509);

        // T6: falling edge, and a one-cycle pulse with both edges enabled.
        apb_write(A_FALL, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1600);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd1601);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, OK, 32'd1602);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1603);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1604);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1605);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0001);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, OK, 32'd1606);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1607);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1608);

        // T7: high level sets again after a clear; an edge does not.
        apb_write(A_FALL, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1700);
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1701);
        apb_write(A_HIGH, 32'h0000_0004, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1702);
        apb_write(A_IEN,  32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1703);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1704);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0005);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0005, OK, 32'd1705);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd1706);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0005, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1707);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0004, OK, 32'd1708);
        tick(32'd3);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0004, OK, 32'd1709);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0001);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0004, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1710);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1711);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1712);

        // T8: low level.
        apb_write(A_HIGH, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1800);
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1801);
        apb_write(A_LOW,  32'h0000_0008, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1802);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0008, OK, 32'd1803);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0008, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1804);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0008, OK, 32'd1805);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0008);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0008, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1806);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1807);
        apb_write(A_LOW, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1808);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1809);

        // T9: several pending bits, clear some only, strobed bytes only.
        pat = (32'h0000_0233 | hb) & PINS;
        apb_write(A_RISE, pat, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1900);
        set_pins(pat);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, pat, OK, 32'd1901);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'b0000, OK, 32'd1902);
        apb_read(A_STAT, pat, OK, 32'd1903);
        e = pat & ~32'h0000_FF00;
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'b0010, OK, 32'd1904);
        apb_read(A_STAT, e, OK, 32'd1905);
        e = e & ~32'h0000_0011;
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0011, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1906);
        apb_read(A_STAT, e, OK, 32'd1907);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_00EE, 4'b1110, OK, 32'd1908);
        apb_read(A_STAT, e, OK, 32'd1909);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1910);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1911);
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd1912);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd1913);

        // T10: a detection on the edge of a clear keeps the bit set.
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0003, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2000);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0003);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0003, OK, 32'd2001);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0003, OK, 32'd2002);
        apb_write_pins(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0003, 4'hF, OK, 32'h0000_0001, 32'd2003);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, OK, 32'd2004);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2005);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd2006);
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2007);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        tick(32'd2);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd2008);

        // T11: the interrupt mask.
        apb_write(A_RISE, 32'h0000_0006, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2100);
        apb_write(A_IEN,  32'h0000_0000, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2101);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0002);
        tick(32'd2);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2102);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0002, OK, 32'd2103);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2104);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2105);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0003, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2106);
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd2107);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0001, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2108);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2109);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0002, 4'h0, OK, 32'd2110);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2111);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0002, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2112);
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd2113);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0002, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2114);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2115);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd2116);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0006);
        tick(32'd2);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2117);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0004, OK, 32'd2118);
        apb_write(A_IEN, 32'h0000_0006, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2119);
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd2120);
        apb_write(A_STAT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2121);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2122);
        apb_write(A_RISE, hb, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2123);
        apb_write(A_IEN,  hb, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2124);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0006 | hb);
        idle_cycle;
        #1;
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2125);
        idle_cycle;
        #1;
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd2126);
        apb_read(A_STAT, hb, OK, 32'd2127);
        apb_write(A_STAT, hb, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2128);
        chk_irq(1'b0, 32'd2129);
        apb_read(A_STAT, 32'h0000_0000, OK, 32'd2130);

        // T12: reset again with state set.
        apb_write(A_DATA_OUT, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2200);
        apb_write(A_DIR,      32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2201);
        apb_write(A_HIGH,     32'h0000_0002, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2202);
        apb_write(A_IEN,      32'h0000_0002, 4'hF, OK, 32'd2203);
        chk_irq(1'b1, 32'd2204);
        check_outs(32'd2205);
        set_pins(32'h0000_0000);
        do_reset(32'd2210);
        read_all_zero(32'd2220);

        done = 1'b1;
    end
endmodule

module apb_gpio_tb;
    wire        done8;
    wire        done32;
    wire [31:0] p8;
    wire [31:0] f8;
    wire [31:0] p32;
    wire [31:0] f32;
    reg  [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    reg  [31:0] passed;
    reg  [31:0] failed;

    apb_gpio_tb_core #(.N(8))  u_n8  (.done(done8),  .n_pass(p8),  .n_fail(f8));
    apb_gpio_tb_core #(.N(32)) u_n32 (.done(done32), .n_pass(p32), .n_fail(f32));

    initial begin
        nonce  = 512'd0;
        passed = 32'd0;
        failed = 32'd0;
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = 512'd0;
        wait (done8 && done32);
        #1;
        passed = p8 + p32;
        failed = f8 + f32;
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

    initial begin
        #2000000;
        $error("apb_gpio_tb: timeout before both test cores finished");
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, p8 + p32, f8 + f32 + 32'd1);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
